{
	title: 'Session ids in model text link to any existing session',
	spec: 'A session id in model text (answers and thinking, outside code) is a link when that session exists, open or closed: bare "06-lbs" opens the session, "06-lbs#u2" its block (task d92). Clicking a closed session reopens it, as /go does. Text that only looks like an id, such as "64-bit" or "3-day", stays text unless a session by that name exists. The host keeps the set of all session ids in memory: one sessions/ directory listing at startup (names only, no metadata), plus each session as it is created; sessions are never deleted, so the set only grows. A client gets the whole set in its connect snapshot and each new id as an event; both clients fill markdown.state.sessions from it instead of from open tabs. Web and terminal behave alike (terminal: OSC 8 to webUrl). Test: a closed session id links; "64-bit" stays text.',
	status: 'planned',
	notes: [
		'Scale: the whole id set is sent on every client connect, about 7 bytes per id: 286 sessions is about 2 KB, 10x is about 20 KB, but a million sessions is about 7 MB at startup and on each first load (more with markup). If that ever matters, send only recent ids and resolve older ones on demand.'
	],
	needs: ['d92'],
	foldInto: ['d92']
}
